00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:28.450
So does that preclude someone, for instance, from uploading their Hacker Public Radio episode to other places, like for instance, their personal blog or a YouTube channel?

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:29.450
No, not at all.

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:36.330
You know, it's as if you were relicensing a piece of software like it is Creative Commons

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:37.330
when you upload it.

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:41.250
You have to have the permission to upload it under a Creative Commons license.

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:44.290
So obviously you can't do commercial music, you can't do stuff you don't own.

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:48.930
But if it is yours, you put it on Hacker Public Radio, you can put it on your website under

00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:50.670
any license you choose.

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:53.610
That would not of course revoke the one that's on Hacker.

00:23:53.610 --> 00:23:58.330
So if someone wanted to copy it under Creative Commons and you didn't like that, you know,

00:23:58.330 --> 00:24:02.610
can go to the one on Hacker Public Radio because that was the license it was released under.

00:24:02.610 --> 00:24:06.690
There's nothing precluding you doing that, but something to keep in mind is, and this

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:13.370
has come up in the past, Hacker Public Radio is not a podcast aggregation service.

00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:17.690
So don't take your podcast, you recorded somewhere else and say, I'll just upload this

00:24:17.690 --> 00:24:18.890
to Hacker Public Radio.

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:22.410
It should be information recorded for Hacker.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:27.810
Now if you have a section, if you record a podcast with another thing and you cut a piece

00:24:27.810 --> 00:24:32.170
out and you make some commentary and put it in there, that's generally okay.

00:24:32.170 --> 00:24:33.930
Or you can talk to the community.

00:24:33.930 --> 00:24:40.090
A lot of times if someone has a new podcast, you can talk to them about putting it on and

00:24:40.090 --> 00:24:43.330
then bringing it to the Hacker Public Radio community.

00:24:43.330 --> 00:24:45.570
But you can't continue that.

00:24:45.570 --> 00:24:48.770
You can't use their distribution network to distribute your podcast.

00:24:48.770 --> 00:24:54.610
You can bring it up as a thing that HPR may be interested in, but that should not be a

